---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from 'astro:env/client';
---

<Doc
  title={`Support | ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`Help with ${APP_NAME}, answers to common questions, and how to report a word.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} is a drawing game that lives inside iMessage. You get
      a word to draw, you send the drawing into the conversation, and
      your friend guesses it whenever they pick up their phone.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>How do I install it?</h3>
    <p>
      Open any Messages conversation and tap the App Store icon next
      to the text field. Search for {APP_NAME} and tap it to turn the
      game on.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I play?</h3>
    <p>
      Open a Messages conversation, tap the {APP_NAME} icon from the
      row of iMessage apps below your text field, draw the word you're
      given, and send the drawing back for the other player to guess.
    </p>

    <h3>Why didn't my drawing send?</h3>
    <p>
      The game rides on iMessage, so iMessage needs to be on and
      connected before your drawing will reach your friend. Check
      Settings, Messages, and your signal, then try again.
    </p>

    <h3>Where did my purchased pack go?</h3>
    <p>
      Open the pack screen inside {APP_NAME} and tap Restore Purchases.
      If it still doesn't come back, check under Settings, Apple ID,
      Subscriptions that you're signed in with the Apple ID that
      bought the pack.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I report a word?</h3>
    <p>
      Tap Report on the word, and a pre-filled email opens for you to
      send. We'll have a look when it arrives.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="doc__aside">
    Details on how we handle data live in the <SiteLink href="/privacy">privacy policy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    If you're still stuck, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>&#8288;.
  </p>
</Doc>
